== type meta
type meta $i                   bare int
type meta $ty                  typed int
type meta $no                  noted {}
type meta $tno                 typednoted int
type meta $s                   bare {}
représentation : list          bare list
représentation : dict          bare dict
le résultat est une somme      typed
== exigences d'un argument
fb $i                          {} {}
fb $ty                         ERREUR argument "x": expected a bare value but got a typed value (int)
fb $no                         ERREUR argument "x": expected a bare value but got a noted value "3"
fb $tno                        ERREUR argument "x": expected a bare value but got a typednoted value (int)
ft $i                          ERREUR argument "x": expected a typed value but got a bare value "2"
ft $ty                         int {}
ft $no                         ERREUR argument "x": expected a typed value but got a noted value "3"
ft $tno                        ERREUR argument "x": expected a typed value but got a typednoted value (int)
fn $i                          ERREUR argument "x": expected a noted value but got a bare value "2"
fn $ty                         ERREUR argument "x": expected a noted value but got a typed value (int)
fn $no                         {} mm
fn $tno                        ERREUR argument "x": expected a noted value but got a typednoted value (int)
ftn $i                         ERREUR argument "x": expected a typednoted value but got a bare value "2"
ftn $ty                        ERREUR argument "x": expected a typednoted value but got a typed value (int)
ftn $no                        ERREUR argument "x": expected a typednoted value but got a noted value "3"
ftn $tno                       int mm
fany $i                        {} {}
fany $ty                       int {}
fany $no                       {} mm
fany $tno                      int mm
fa $i                          ERREUR argument "x": expected annotee but got a bare value "2"
fa $ty                         ERREUR argument "x": expected annotee but got a typed value (int)
fa $no                         {} mm
fa $tno                        int mm
le cast de l'appel d'abord     ERREUR argument "x": expected a bare value but got a typed value (int)
== any : l'identité
type cast any (typée, notée)   int mm
type cast any (nue)            {} {}
{any}$x                        int mm
set {any}v                     int mm
list.any                       {{} {}} {{} this} {int mm}
dict.any                       a {{} {}} b {int mm}
== set et conteneurs
set {typed}x                   int {}
set {typed}x 5                 ERREUR expected a typed value but got a bare value "5"
pas de contrat                 {} {}
list.typed                     {int {}} {double {}}
list.typed refuse une nue      ERREUR expected a typed value but got a bare value "5"
list.bare                      {{} {}} {{} {}}
list.bare refuse une typée     ERREUR expected a bare value but got a typed value (int)
dict.typed                     a {int {}} b {double {}}
type cast typed                int {}
type cast typed 5              ERREUR expected a typed value but got a bare value "5"
== unions
noted | typednoted             ok
bare | any : refusée           ERREUR union: alternatives a and b can take the same value, so the value could not tell which one it is; a union must be disjoint. Write a sum with "," to tag the alternatives
int | bare : refusée           ERREUR union: alternatives i and b can take the same value, so the value could not tell which one it is; a union must be disjoint. Write a sum with "," to tag the alternatives
noms réservés                  ERREUR type "typed" is already defined
== forme canonique d'une valeur nue
canonic 5                      {{bare}5} bare 1
canonic {a b}                  {{bare}{a b}} bare 1
canonic {}                     {{bare}{}} bare 1
type parse {typed}5            ERREUR expected a typed value but got a bare value "5"
